# Creative SoundBlaster X Katana USB Audio Driver
# This rule ensures our specialized katana-usb-audio driver binds to the device
# instead of the generic snd-usb-audio driver

# Katana device: USB ID 041e:3247
#
# snd-usb-audio matches this device through its static, generic audio-class
# table rather than through a dynamic ID, which rules out the obvious approach:
#   - remove_id only drops IDs that were added via new_id, so writing the
#     Katana's ID to it silently succeeds and changes nothing.
#   - new_id on this driver is redundant (041e:3247 is already in its static
#     id_table) and cannot claim an interface that snd-usb-audio has already
#     bound, because the driver core skips any device with a driver attached.
#
# So unbind explicitly, then bind. %k is the interface's kernel name, e.g.
# "1-2:1.0", which is what the bind/unbind sysfs attributes expect.
#
# Matching per-interface rather than on the parent usb_device is deliberate:
# the usb_device's add event is emitted before its interfaces are registered,
# so a rule that globs for them can find nothing. This is tighter but still not
# a hard guarantee, since an interface's own add event also precedes its probe.
#
# Interfaces other than 0 (AudioControl) and 1 (AudioStream OUT) are rejected by
# this driver's probe, so the bind write fails harmlessly for them.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_interface", \
  ATTRS{idVendor}=="041e", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3247", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo %k > /sys/bus/usb/drivers/snd-usb-audio/unbind 2>/dev/null; \
    echo %k > /sys/bus/usb/drivers/katana_usb_audio/bind 2>/dev/null'"
